  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-285776" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Safe and Dignified Burials in Sierra Leone (Kambia District)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ministry of Health and Sanitation in Sierra Leone reported on 21th   October that there have been 3,345 confirmed cases of Ebola since May although the number of unreported cases is thought to be much higher.  The number of fatalities is 1,001 giving a death rate of 30%.  
As shown in the recent FOCUS 1000/CRS/ UNICEF KAP survey, 37% of people infected with Ebola attributed their infection to attendance at a funeral. This is due to the large number of people in attendance and traditional practices of preparing and burying the body.  This highlights the importance of safe burial practices. The strategy for this proposal is based on the priorities outlined in the GoSL Accelerated Ebola Outbreak Response Plan, and the WHO Ebola Response Plan.</narrative>
  </description>
